    {
      "id": "1460063893090209803",
      "type": "Default",
      "timestamp": "2026-01-11T19:12:38.788-05:00",
      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "I tested WMI v10 (1fa82260-1171-4db5-9968-d34ce2e14694) for about 30 minutes during a clear daytime drive.\nCompared to v8, lateral behavior feels just as smooth and confident—very much like an experienced human driver. Really nice work there.\nIn experimental E2E longitudinal mode, however, it seems to keep more following distance than necessary. At times it felt like the car behind might get impatient \uD83D\uDE05\nBecause of the large gap, many vehicles kept cutting in front, which made the experience a bit less comfortable in traffic.\nFor now, I’ll continue using v8 as my daily driving model, but I’m interested to see how v10’s longitudinal behavior evolves.",
      "author": {
